From 12ddbd3103de51c251ff46229a6c86b4fa6662c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:40:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 40/44] libretro: forget the loaded game on unload

retro_unload_game shut the system down but left game_loaded set. With
OpenGL, the frontend's context_destroy then released the renderer through
the destroyed GPU (null dereference), and the next game's context_reset
skipped loading it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GBZiGZJLWikH7o79f84GTm
---
 src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp b/src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp
index 2b5fd1d..011d0e6 100644
--- a/src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/citra_libretro.cpp
@@ -642,6 +642,9 @@ bool retro_load_game(const struct retro_game_info* info) {
 void retro_unload_game() {
     LOG_DEBUG(Frontend, "Unloading game...");
     Core::System::GetInstance().Shutdown();
+    // The GPU is gone now: context_destroy must not release the OpenGL renderer
+    // through it, and the next context_reset must boot the next game.
+    emu_instance->game_loaded = false;
 }
 
 unsigned retro_get_region() {
